{{Quote|I have a camtono of Beskar waiting for you upon the delivery of the asset.|"The Client," to "the Mandalorian"|audio=Client-camtono.flac|<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref>}}
A '''camtono''' also known as a '''camtono bag''' was a kind of security container for storing valuables. Notable users of camtonos included "[[the Client]]," [[Cobb Vanth]], [[Willrow Hood]] and the [[Pyke Syndicate]].

==Description==
[[File:OpenCamtono-TMCh3.png|thumb|left|250px|An open camtono with beskar]]
The camtono was a cylindrical box consisting of a fixed frame, three movable panels hinged at the bottom and locked shut at the top, and a "lid" part. That lid boasted control buttons and a rotary cylindric piece featuring a handle. Buttons disengaged the locks, causing the side panels to fall open and thus granting access to the contents.<ref name="Chapter 3" />

Camtonos could notably be used to store [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]], explosives,<ref name="Comes a Stranger" /> precious metals or [[spice]]. They could be easily transported by holding the handle,<ref name="Chapter 3" /> although they were small enough to be tucked under the average [[humanoid]]'s [[Limb|arm]]. Camtonos came in various colors, including [[Color|while]],<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|camtono-case|camtono case}}</ref> jade, and sapphire.<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref> 

==History==
{{Quote|Mando, enjoy your rewards. Buy a camtono of spice.|Greef Karga to "the Mandalorian"|<ref name="Chapter 3" />}}
[[File:WillrowHood-TESB.png|thumb|right|200px|Willrow Hood carried a camtono in Cloud City.]]
A [[Gender|male]] [[human]] named [[Willrow Hood]]<ref name="Card Trader">{{SWCT|set=Topps Choice|cardname=Willrow Hood}}</ref> was seen transporting a camtono under his arm at multiple points in his life,<ref name="SW22">[[Star Wars (2015) 22|''Star Wars'' (2015) 22]]</ref><ref name="SWU">''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]''</ref> including when [[Baron Administrator]] [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] told the people of [[Cloud City]] to evacuate due to the [[Escape from Cloud City|Imperial threat]].<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref>

By [[3 ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate">{{OutlawsDate}}</ref> a camtono had been stored in a [[flooded cave]] over looking [[Kadùa Village]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[moon]] [[Toshara]].<ref name="Outlaws" /> By the same [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="OutlawsDate" /> a sapphire colored camtono had been stashed in a container on the Outer Rim [[planet]] [[Akiva]] at [[Mozampa Farm]] in the [[Myrra Valley]] region.<ref name="Outlaws" />

{{Gamemechanics|Star Wars Outlaws|canon=1}}
In 3 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate" /> the [[thief]] [[Kay Vess]] found and looted both camtonos on Toshara and Akiva. Around the same time, [[Nix]], Vess's [[merqaal]] companion, found a jade colored camtono and stashed it in his nest aboard the ''[[Trailblazer]]'', Vess's [[EML-850 light freighter]]. Vess later found the camtono while cleaning up Nix's mess.<ref name="Outlaws" />
{{Endgame}}

Shortly after the [[Battle of Endor]] and [[Imperial Military]]'s withdrawal from [[Tatooine]], the [[Mining Collective]] arrived in the small town of [[Freetown|Mos Pelgo]]. As he escaped into [[desert]], [[Sheriff]] [[Cobb Vanth]] stole a camtono from the collective. This contained a number of [[silicax oxalate]] crystals, which he used to buy a [[Boba Fett's armor|set of]] [[Mandalorian armor]] from [[Jawa]]s, who stole the armor from [[Boba Fett]]. He then returned to Mos Pelgo and, using the armor, [[Liberation of Mos Pelgo|liberated]] the town.<ref name="Chapter 9" />

In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Mandalorian date">{{MandoDate|3}}</ref> "[[the Client]]" hired the [[bounty hunter]] known as [[Din Djarin|"the Mandalorian"]] to recover a [[Din Grogu|child]] on the [[planet]] [[Arvala-7]] in exchange for a camtono of [[beskar]].<ref name="Chapter 1" /> Having accomplished the mission, the Mandalorian received the beskar and transported it to his [[The Tribe|tribe's]] [[Nevarro Mandalorian covert|covert]], where he provided the contents inside to [[the Armorer]] to forge a full cuirass. Later, when the Mandalorian expressed doubts about the ethics of the Client, [[Greef Karga]], head of the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]], suggested that he should forget about it and buy himself a camtono of [[spice]].<ref name="Chapter 3" />

The [[Pyke Syndicate]] used camtonos to store [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] and explosives. One camtono with explosives was used to cause an [[Destruction of Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|explosion]] in the cantina [[Garsa Fwip's Sanctuary|Sanctuary]].<ref name="Comes a Stranger" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|For those who know, they'll appreciate it. For those who don't it just looks like a cool ''Star Wars'' thing.|[[Jon Favreau]], on the camtono's appearance in ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''|<ref name="Connections (Disney Gallery: The Mandalorian)">{{DisneyGallery|Connections}}</ref>}}
The camtono prop in ''[[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|The Empire Strikes Back]]'' was an ordinary ice cream maker. This was noticed by fans, and the character apparently fleeing Cloud City clutching an ice cream machine developed a humorous cult following.<ref name="SWBlog">{{Blog|Yossarian|2|The Story of Willrow Hood, Or: Now You Know What That Big White Thing Is.}}</ref><ref name="Insider49">{{InsiderCite|49|The Ultimate Empire Strikes Back Insider's Guide|The Ultimate ''Empire Strikes Back'' Insider's Guide}}</ref> The creators of [[Star Wars: The Mandalorian|''The Mandalorian'']] took the name from a viral internet video where a toddler mispronounces "ice cream" as "camtono."<ref name="Camtono">{{YouTube|video=pc-Qq6Aaf3Q|text=Little girl likes "comsonose"|channel=channel/UCdAeRRjq6vjnAkxatZVxxxg|name=RM Videos}}</ref><ref name="Mandalorian Vanity Fair">{{WebCite|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2019/11/the-mandalorian-boba-fett-ig-88-familiar|text=''The Mandalorian'' Feels Familiar, but the Star Wars Show Is Pulling a Jedi Mind Trick|author=Anthony Breznican|date=2019-11-11|archivedate=20191122111214}}</ref>

